# macOS DMG After Revisions

After making any code changes that affect the packaged desktop app, always rebuild the macOS installer from the project root:

```bash
npm run dmg
```

This includes changes to frontend (`src/`, `dist/`), server (`server.ts`, `desktop/`), Electron (`electron/`), build config (`package.json`, `vite.config.*`, electron-builder `build` field), or bundled runtime scripts (`scripts/prepare-desktop-runtime.mjs`, `scripts/electron-before-pack.cjs`, `scripts/build-dmg.mjs`).

On macOS, confirm the output exists when the build finishes:

- `release/Creative Asset Extractor-1.0.0-universal.dmg`

If the version in `package.json` changes, the DMG filename will use the new version — check `release/*.dmg` for the latest file.

- Do not skip the DMG rebuild when shipping or revising the desktop package.
- `npm run dmg` is macOS-only; on other platforms, note that the DMG must be built on a Mac.
- Run `npm run dev` after the DMG build as well (see dev-server rule).
